From 6cbbc62493e1baa7ec12e0dc0907348d89937756 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:12:08 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 37/44] GE census: describe a draw only when a feature is first
 seen

Formatting every draw's description cost more than the draw: a battle ran
at about real time with the census on. The description is now made only
for a feature's first hit, the scene being counted is kept at hand, and the
file is written every 600 frames, so a run stopped at a time limit loses
less. Battles run about 2.5 times faster than with the first version.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 host/gpu/ge_census.cpp | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 host/gpu/ge_census.hpp |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/host/gpu/ge_census.cpp b/host/gpu/ge_census.cpp
index 6bb348a..4c78d21 100644
--- a/host/gpu/ge_census.cpp
+++ b/host/gpu/ge_census.cpp
